<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Clemens returns five weeks after intake. He has had four grief therapy sessions; he has told the story of his wife&apos;s last evening, held an imaginal conversation with her, and looked through one photograph album. He sleeps about five hours. The passing thoughts of joining her have not come in the last two weeks. He had chest tightness once more, three weeks ago, walking fast up a steep hill, gone within three minutes of stopping. The CT coronary angiogram this morning showed a calcium score of 410 and a 25 to 49 percent narrowing of the main artery at the front of the heart, with no blockage. He smokes about eight cigars a day. Having seen the pictures of his arteries, he says he is ready to try to stop. He had a twinge in the right big toe last week that settled in a day. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Grief therapy</td><td>Four sessions; PG-13-R 37</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No thoughts of death for two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Chest</td><td>One episode three weeks ago on a steep hill</td></tr><tr><td>CT coronary angiogram</td><td>Calcium score 410; CAD-RADS 2, nonobstructive</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>About eight cigars a day; ready to quit</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

