    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Persistent yearning for his wife, broken sleep, low mood and withdrawal from friends and work, a year after her death; cause under evaluation</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z63.4</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to his wife&apos;s documented death a year before; resolved into the diagnosis of prolonged grief disorder at the consultation. Not a claim about his real grief.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Prolonged grief disorder (DSM-5-TR): more than 12 months after his wife&apos;s death, daily yearning and preoccupation with her, with intense emotional pain, a sense that part of himself has died, avoidance of reminders, loneliness, difficulty taking up his work and life again, and a feeling that life is meaningless; PG-13-R 41; major depression not present</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F43.81</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the consultation, anchored to his documented bereavements. Not a claim about his real mental health; the roster&apos;s bipolar lead is not used.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Tobacco use disorder, cigars: about fifteen cigars a day, smoking since boyhood, some smoke inhaled; first cigar within thirty minutes of waking</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F17.290</td><td>S — Synthetic modern coding anchored to his documented smoking since boyhood.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Chest tightness on climbing steep hills, twice in the past month, easing within five minutes of rest; none at rest; cause under evaluation</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R07.89</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting symptom; resolved into a diagnosis at five weeks after CT coronary angiography. Not a claim about his real heart in 1905; his documented chest pain began in 1909.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Coronary artery disease, nonobstructive (CAD-RADS 2: 25 to 49 percent narrowing of the proximal left anterior descending artery; coronary calcium score 410), with exertional chest tightness that has not recurred on treatment; treated with a statin, aspirin and stopping smoking</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>I25.10</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at five weeks. Not a claim about his real coronary arteries.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-6">
    <td>Gout, recurrent flares of the big toe since his late fifties, two in the past year; serum urate 8.6 mg/dL; no tophi</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>M10.9</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis anchored to his documented gout.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

